<h2>10. APIs and services used</h2>
<p>
  For transparency, here is every external API EchoX talks to. All of them are free and
  public, and all requests are made directly from your browser.
</p>
<ul class="api-list">
  <li>
    <strong>Audius API v1</strong> —
    <a href="https://api.audius.co/v1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">api.audius.co/v1</a><br />
    Used for: trending tracks (<code>/tracks/trending</code>), search
    (<code>/tracks/search</code>), artist catalogues
    (<code>/users/handle/&#123;handle&#125;/tracks</code>) and full-track audio streaming
    (<code>/tracks/&#123;id&#125;/stream</code>).<br />
    Access: read endpoints need no API key; the app identifies itself with
    <code>app_name=echox</code>. Free tier: 10 requests/second and 500,000 requests/month.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Apple iTunes Search API</strong> —
    <a href="https://itunes.apple.com/search" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">itunes.apple.com/search</a>
    and
    <a href="https://itunes.apple.com/lookup" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">itunes.apple.com/lookup</a><br />
    Used for: 30-second preview clips (<code>previewUrl</code>), artwork
    (<code>artworkUrl100</code>), track metadata and artist track listings. No key required;
    the endpoint is public and rate-limited.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Deezer public API</strong> —
    <a href="https://api.deezer.com/search" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">api.deezer.com/search</a><br />
    Used for: a second world-wide catalogue of 30-second preview clips
    (<code>preview</code>), artwork and artist top tracks
    (<code>/artist/&#123;id&#125;/top</code>). No key required. Deezer does not send CORS
    headers, so the app reads this API through JSONP.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Apple Podcasts (iTunes Search API)</strong> —
    <a href="https://itunes.apple.com/search" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">itunes.apple.com/search</a><br />
    Used for: podcast episodes (<code>media=podcast&amp;entity=podcastEpisode</code>),
    episode artwork and audio (<code>previewUrl</code>), plus more episodes from the same show.
    No key required.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Radio Browser API</strong> —
    <a href="https://api.radio-browser.info" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">api.radio-browser.info</a><br />
    Used for: live online radio stations, their stream URLs and logos. A free, community-run,
    keyless directory. Only streams served over HTTPS are shown, and the app links to the
    broadcaster's own stream.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>YouTube Data API v3</strong> —
    <a href="https://developers.google.com/youtube/v3" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">developers.google.com/youtube/v3</a><br />
    Used for: music video search (<code>/search</code>), the most-popular music video chart
    (<code>/videos?chart=mostPopular</code>) and public video metadata such as the description,
    view, like and comment counts (<code>/videos?part=snippet,statistics</code>). Requests are
    made directly from your browser with a public API key restricted to this site. No YouTube
    account or personal credential is used.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>YouTube IFrame Player API</strong> —
    <a href="https://developers.google.com/youtube/iframe_api_reference" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">developers.google.com/youtube/iframe_api_reference</a><br />
    Used for: playing embedded music videos with YouTube's own player. Playback depends on the
    uploader allowing embeds and is subject to YouTube's terms of service; Google may set
    cookies or collect data as described in its privacy policy.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Astro</strong> —
    <a href="https://astro.build" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">astro.build</a><br />
    Not an API, but the static site framework EchoX is built with. The whole app ships as
    plain HTML, CSS and JavaScript.
  </li>
</ul>
<p>
  No Spotify or Apple Music account API is used, and YouTube is only accessed through its
  public Data API and embedded player — never through a user account. No music or video files
  are downloaded by EchoX, and no personal credentials are stored by the site. The YouTube API
  key is a public, site-restricted key that ships with the page; it is not a user secret. Deezer
  previews, podcast episodes and YouTube videos are streamed exactly as their services provide
  them; live radio is played straight from the broadcaster's stream.
</p>

